# Normal setup does not require copying this file: `researchwiki init` creates
# or updates the automatically loaded `.env` directly and restricts it to mode
# 0600. Use this template when configuring `.env` manually:
#   cp .env.template .env && chmod 600 .env
#
# Use it also to create a named profile. An explicit `--env-file` must already
# exist so a misspelled path cannot silently fall back to the root `.env`:
#   cp .env.template .env.openai && chmod 600 .env.openai
#   researchwiki --env-file .env.openai init
#   researchwiki --env-file .env.openai status
#
# `init` writes the model-config selector for the provider you choose. Add the
# matching credential below before running `researchwiki doctor --probe`.
# Do not export routing variables in the parent shell when using --env-file;
# explicit profiles reject them rather than silently using the wrong provider.

# OpenAI (also used for Gemini and other OpenAI-compatible providers).
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# Anthropic.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Local-model and chat-relay setups require no API key.

# Advanced: custom OpenAI-compatible endpoints normally belong in their model
# config. This environment variable is available as a temporary override. Use
# only endpoints you trust because the API key and paper content are sent there.
# RW_LLM_BASE_URL=https://your-provider.example/v1
